$ =====================================================================
$ RBE3 TEST SERIES -- Deck 05: independent-grid ROTATION component is
$ silently ignored (separate gap from the two DX_BAR/WRITE_L1J_456
$ bugs -- found while reviewing RBE3_PROC.f90's WRITE_L1J_123/456).
$
$ Independent grids 501, 502 sit COLLINEAR along the element's local
$ x-axis (y=z=0 for both), so their translations carry NO information
$ about twist (rotation) about that axis -- the standard NASTRAN
$ RBE3 documentation explicitly recommends adding a ROTATION
$ component to one independent grid ("Ci"=4/5/6) in exactly this
$ situation, to stabilize/define that rigid-body mode. Grid 503 does
$ that here: it contributes ONLY comp 4 (Rx) to the independent set,
$ weight=5.0, with a prescribed rotation of 0.5 via SPC.
$
$ REFC=4 -- only the reference grid's Rx is dependent, isolating
$ this one row cleanly.
$
$ RBE3_PROC.f90 never reads CDOF_I(4)/(5)/(6) anywhere (neither in
$ the EBAR_YZ/ZX/XY sums nor in WRITE_L1J_456) -- independent grid
$ rotation components are accepted by the bulk-data reader
$ (BD_RBE3.f90 places no restriction on Ci) but have ZERO effect on
$ the constraint math. Combined with collinear grids 501/502 driving
$ EBAR_YZ to (near) zero, RBE3_PROC.f90 falls back to hard-setting
$ the pivot coefficient to 1.0 (see lines ~353-360) instead of using
$ grid 503's contribution at all.
$
$ Expected (per NASTRAN's own documented stabilization technique):
$   R1 (grid 500) = 0.5   (the reference should pick up the
$   independent grid's prescribed rotation, since it's the only
$   information available about twist on this collinear axis)
$
$ Actual (as-coded, MYSTRAN dev branch):
$   R1 (grid 500) = 0.0   -- grid 503's rotation input is completely
$   discarded; MYSTRAN reports zero twist no matter what value is
$   prescribed on grid 503's Rx.
$ =====================================================================
SOL 101
CEND
DISP = ALL
SPC = 1
BEGIN BULK
$
GRID,500,,0.,0.,0.
$
$ Collinear independent translation grids (along local/global x).
GRID,501,,-3.,0.,0.
GRID,502,,3.,0.,0.
$
$ Stabilizing independent grid: contributes ONLY its Rx rotation.
GRID,503,,1.,0.,0.
$
GRID,400,,5.,5.,5.
GRID,401,,6.,5.,5.
MAT1,1,1.,,0.
PROD,1,1,1.
CROD,96,1,400,401
$
$ REFC=4: only Rx of grid 500 is dependent.
$ Group 1: grids 501,502, comp=123 (translations), weight=1.0.
$ Group 2: grid 503, comp=4 (rotation), weight=5.0 -- the
$ NASTRAN-recommended stabilizing DOF for a collinear independent set.
RBE3    30              500     4       1.0     123     501     502     +A1
+A1     5.0     4       503
$
$ Collinear grids: translations pinned to zero (irrelevant to the Rx
$ fit either way, since Dy=Dz=0 for both).
SPC,1,501,123456,0.
SPC,1,502,123456,0.
$
$ Stabilizing grid: prescribe Rx=0.5, pin everything else.
SPC,1,503,123,0.
SPC,1,503,4,0.5
SPC,1,503,56,0.
$
$ Reference grid: only Rx (comp4) is dependent -- fix the rest.
SPC,1,500,12356,0.
$
SPC,1,400,123456,0.
$ (grid 401 deliberately left unconstrained -- gives the model a
$  genuine free DOF so MSC Nastran has an L-set to solve; it's an
$  unloaded dummy CROD end, disconnected from the RBE3 under test, so
$  this has no effect on the RBE3 results.)
$
ENDDATA
